  "question": "1) Background / Context\n\nThe project aims to develop a data analysis system based on Shakespeare's complete works, enhancing literary study through data-driven insights. This dataset provides rich, historical text data suitable for developing predictive models and other analytical tools.\n\n2) Objectives\n\nThe primary objective is to predict the speaking character for each line within Shakespeare's works. This involves processing and analyzing text data to create predictive models that accurately assign lines to characters. The project also seeks to make Shakespeare's texts more interactive and accessible for academic and personal study.\n\n3) Stakeholders & Users\n\n- Stakeholders:\n  - Educational Institutions: Enhance learning and analysis of Shakespeare.\n  - Literary Researchers: Provide tools for advanced literary analysis.\n\n- Users:\n  - Students: Use the system to study and understand Shakespeare's works.\n  - Academics and Researchers: Conduct research and literary analysis.\n\n4) Functional Descriptions\n\n- Data Processing: Ingest and parse Shakespeare's text data, storing it in a structured database format.\n- Prediction Model: Develop and implement algorithms to predict the speaker of each line based on textual analysis.\n- Search and Query: Allow users to search works by characters, scenes, and specific lines.\n- Interactive Analysis: Provide interactive tools to explore the relationships between characters and text.\n- Data Management: Include functionalities for administrators to update and maintain the database.\n\n5) Non-Functional Descriptions\n\n- Performance: Ensure efficient processing of large text datasets, supporting real-time interaction.\n- Scalability: Accommodate an increasing number of users and data entries.\n- Usability: Design a user-friendly interface for easy navigation and exploration of Shakespeare's works.\n- Security: Implement measures to protect the integrity and confidentiality of the dataset.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: schemabench_0129\nCREATE TABLE `play` (\n  `play_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `genre` varchar(100) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `year_written` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `source_text` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`play_id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `character` (\n  `character_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `character_name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `alias` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `description` text DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`character_id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `uk_character_name` (`character_name`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `scene` (\n  `scene_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `play_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `act_number` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `scene_number` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `scene_title` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`scene_id`),\n  KEY `play_id` (`play_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `scene_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`play_id`) REFERENCES `play` (`play_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `line` (\n  `line_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `scene_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `line_number` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `speaker_character_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `line_text` text NOT NULL,\n  `predicted_character_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `prediction_confidence` decimal(5,4) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`line_id`),\n  KEY `scene_id` (`scene_id`),\n  KEY `speaker_character_id` (`speaker_character_id`),\n  KEY `predicted_character_id` (`predicted_character_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `line_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`scene_id`) REFERENCES `scene` (`scene_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `line_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`speaker_character_id`) REFERENCES `character` (`character_id`) ON DELETE SET NULL ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `line_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`predicted_character_id`) REFERENCES `character` (`character_id`) ON DELETE SET NULL ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `character_scene` (\n  `character_scene_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `character_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `scene_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `line_count` int(11) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`character_scene_id`),\n  UNIQUE KEY `uk_character_scene` (`character_id`,`scene_id`),\n  KEY `scene_id` (`scene_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `character_scene_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`character_id`) REFERENCES `character` (`character_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `character_scene_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`scene_id`) REFERENCES `scene` (`scene_id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `search_log` (\n  `search_log_id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `searched_at` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `search_type` varchar(50) NOT NULL,\n  `query_text` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `play_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `character_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `scene_id` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`search_log_id`),\n  KEY `play_id` (`play_id`),\n  KEY `character_id` (`character_id`),\n  KEY `scene_id` (`scene_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `search_log_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`play_id`) REFERENCES `play` (`play_id`) ON DELETE SET NULL ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `search_log_ibfk_2` FOREIGN KEY (`character_id`) REFERENCES `character` (`character_id`) ON DELETE SET NULL ON UPDATE CASCADE,\n  CONSTRAINT `search_log_ibfk_3` FOREIGN KEY (`scene_id`) REFERENCES `scene` (`scene_id`) ON DELETE SET NULL ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
